How would you explain the concept of tim:
To explain the concept of time to someone who has never experienced it, I would start by describing time as a way to understand change and the order in which events happen. Time allows us to organize our experiences, knowing what happened first, what came next, and what followed after that.

Imagine if everything around you could change, like a story unfolding. Time helps us track that story, marking moments when things happen. It's like a river flowing, where every moment is a point along the way.

When we talk about time stopping, it can be understood as a pause in that flow. In this scenario, all changes cease;
